---
// src/components/GoodCause.astro
---
<section id="cause">
    <div class="layout">
        <h2>Are you a force for good?</h2>
        <p>
            Thank you for taking on a great cause. But it's hard to do good if
            nobody knows! Your non-profit, charity, or political group deserves
            a soapbox. <a href="/contact">Let me handle that,</a> so you can do the
            rest.
        </p>
        <ul class="features">
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Strategy and Design</h3>
                    <p>
                        Before we build anything, let's determine what your
                        goals are. Every organization has different aims,
                        different stakeholders, and different strategies. Your
                        site needs to be tailored to your cause.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Hosting</h3>
                    <p>
                        Fast, secure, and backed up. I deal with the nerdy stuff
                        so you don't have to worry about it while you're saving
                        the world.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Content Management</h3>
                    <p>
                        I can shepherd and format your content, or you can take
                        the reins with a CMS, including WordPress and headless
                        solutions like Contentful and Sanity.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>News and Calendars</h3>
                    <p>
                        Fundraisers, classes, volunteer drives... Your
                        organization may have a lot of balls in the air, but
                        you'll have an easily updated public calendar to keep
                        track of them all.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Integrations</h3>
                    <p>
                        Keep your site in sync with outside services like
                        Eventbrite, Shopify, and donation platforms.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <!--
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>"Up, up, and away!"</h3>
                    <p>
                        <a href="https://athena-squad.netlify.app/"
                            >Athena Squad</a
                        > is a fictional (thus far) organization devoted to promoting
                        teen science engagement. <a
                            href="https://athena-squad.netlify.app/"
                            >To the stars!</a
                        >
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
        -->
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    #cause {
        background: #FADCDC;
        color: #2B2D42;
        padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
        @media screen and (max-width: 500px) {
            padding: 2rem 0;
        }
        h2 {
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: normal;
            color: #14151F;
        }
        a {
            color: #B22E47;
        }
        .features {
            list-style: none;
            margin: 3rem 0 0 0;
            padding: 0;
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
            gap: 1.5rem;
            @media screen and (max-width: 750px) {
                grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
            }
            @media screen and (max-width: 500px) {
                grid-template-columns: repeat(1, 1fr);
            }
            li {
                background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
                padding: 1.5em;
                border-radius: 8px;
            }
            h3 {
                font-size: 2rem;
                font-weight: normal;
                color: #14151F;
                text-wrap: pretty;
                padding: 0;
                margin: 0;
            }
            p {
                font-size: 1.25rem;
                line-height: 180%;
                margin: 1rem 0;
                text-wrap: pretty;
            }
        }
    }
</style>
